        open ? 'With the stopcock open, both gases can enter the connecting tube. The lighter H₂ particles spread into the opposite bulb sooner than heavier O₂ particles.' : 'The closed stopcock blocks the tube, so H₂ and O₂ remain in separate bulbs.');
